{"id": "EUVD-2026-102269", "enisaUuid": "4cfea26a-2c0d-3785-91cb-8660453943bf", "description": "Zziplib through 0.13.80 contains an out-of-bounds read vulnerability in zzip/mmapped.c that allows attackers to over-read heap memory via a crafted ZIP central directory. Attackers can craft an end-of-central-directory record placing the first entry near the buffer end, causing zzip_disk_entry_strdup_name to read past the buffer and crash the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:10:35", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/zziplib-zip-central-directory-oob-read", "https://github.com/gdraheim/zziplib/blob/f58313c1f65f46bf73f3526d1afd4d6bb46cc4ae/zzip/mmapped.c#L420-L497", "https://github.com/gdraheim/zziplib/blob/f58313c1f65f46bf73f3526d1afd4d6bb46cc4ae/zzip/mmapped.c#L323-L352", "https://github.com/gdraheim/zziplib", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zziplib-through-0.13.80-out-of-bounds-read-via-zzip-disk-findfirst"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5xjw-pf8f-qr57", "CVE-2026-111142"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "038d6917-2198-3bd6-a992-6eff97e8dd06", "product": {"name": "zziplib", "vendor": {"name": "Microsoft"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.13.80"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "495f2b23-b57f-3857-85bc-2b656af6406d", "vendor": {"name": "gdraheim"}}], "isExploited": false}